/*
  Localizable.strings (English)
  MacStats

  The English text is the key (see Sources/MacStats/Localization.swift), so
  en.lproj and tr.lproj must hold exactly the same keys; LocalizationTests
  checks that, and that every L10n.string("…") in the sources has an entry.

  Deliberately NOT localized, and so not listed here:
  - The three-letter menu bar labels CPU, GPU, RAM, DSK, NET, BAT, FAN, TMP:
    the menu bar must stay compact and aligned, and they read as technical
    abbreviations in Turkish too.
  - Unit symbols (B, KB, MB, GB, TB, °C) and the menu bar's compact values
    ("8.2G", "812K"); only their spoken VoiceOver forms are translated.
  - The app name "MacStats" and device or app names reported by macOS.

  Format specifiers: every argument is %@, text. Numbers arrive already
  formatted for the user's region, so "23,4" stays "23,4". Use positional
  forms such as %2$@ to reorder arguments, and %% for a literal percent sign.
*/


